    {
      "question": "e-3619",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "fe6eae0c7b63f61bb75f0df789dc77acffe3c6c7469b94c1a96eb3b01b69586e",
      "new_sha256": "ed414e0e5f6956baf86fdfc58c6c19226e3a07713e1379bc34bbef53ae7f9905",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-3619",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}}{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061{25}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3619.json",
          "file_sha256": "8a7ee392e973cfbe9a6dd2b06a1994e60b3a50cb853a49686cd38380d0672f4c"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1287,
